From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:01:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - immutable mob snapshot for async pathfinding

Audit ENG-8: the async path worker read the live Mob off its owner thread (position, bounding box, pathfindingMalus EnumMap, canStandOnFluid, maxUpStep, getMaxFallDistance, getRandom, and noCollision(mob, box) building an EntityCollisionContext from isDescending/getMainHandItem).

Every mob member the solve reads is now captured on the owner in dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.perf.MobPathSnapshot (captureDetached in PathNavigation.sourbyKickAsyncRecompute). PathFinder.findPath(PathNavigationRegion, MobPathSnapshot, ...) prepares the evaluator with the snapshot and a null mob; Walk/Fly/Swim/Amphibious/Frog evaluators read this.subject() instead of this.mob, collision goes through the snapshot off-thread and the live mob on the owner, level minY comes from the region. The synchronous solve captures the same snapshot lazily on the owner after the prepare chain, keeping the mob's own RandomSource, so the feature-off path is unchanged.

Creaking's navigation refuses the offload: HomeNodeEvaluator reads Creaking.this.getHomePos() outside the Mob API. Sniffer and AmphibiousPathNavigation stay refused as before.

Tests: MobPathSnapshotTest (sealed mob fake, unchanged result after mutation, sync == snapshot, fluid table, border), AsyncPathEvaluatorIsolationTest, AsyncPathRefusalTest.

